  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Can I read fuel level remotely on a Kia Telluride?",
      "a": "Yes, with a DIMO device. The Telemetry API exposes fuel level as a percentage (powertrainFuelSystemRelativeLevel) and in liters (powertrainFuelSystemAbsoluteLevel). The segments query with the refuel mechanism detects where fuel level rises significantly."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I track a Kia Telluride with no connected services?",
      "a": "Use a DIMO device. Once the vehicle is shared with your Developer License, exchange your Developer JWT for a Vehicle JWT through the Token Exchange API, then query the Telemetry API (GraphQL) with that Vehicle JWT."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I detect idling on a Kia Telluride?",
      "a": "Idling detection requires a DIMO device. Call the segments query in the Telemetry API with the idling mechanism, which returns contiguous periods where engine RPM stays in the idle range. You can tune the upper RPM bound with maxIdleRpm, which defaults to 1000."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I verify Kia Telluride mileage?",
      "a": "With a DIMO device supplying the odometer signal, call the Attestation API endpoint POST /v2/attestation/odometer-statement/:tokenId using a Vehicle JWT. You then retrieve the resulting verifiable credential (rawVC) through the Telemetry API."
    }
  ],
  "intro": "DIMO gives developers API access to vehicle-state data: diagnostics, fault codes, battery and fuel health, odometer, and maintenance signals. For the Kia Telluride, 2020 and newer, data comes through a DIMO device, and this coverage has been tested. Vehicle owners consent to and control sharing, so builders get data with clear provenance. DIMO adds vehicle-state depth on top of GPS tracking; it doesn't replace it."
}
